      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Beaver River splits the hamlet, crossed by two vehicle bridges and a central railway trestle.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaver_Falls%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1850s Beaver Falls was entirely farmland owned by the Farneys before selling plots for homes and churches in the 20th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaver_Falls%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 95‑megawatt Beaver Falls Generating Facility, completed in 1995, supplies New York’s grid with power and steam to the nearby Omniafiltra mill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaver_Falls%2C_New_York",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic Lewis Company Mill on the hamlet’s western edge once produced paper but now houses Omniafiltra, an Italian‑owned filtration paper manufacturer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
